  "progressionType": "percentage",
  "progressionNotes": "Every main lift is prescribed at a percentage of your 1RM. Keep the weight and the sets and reps as written.",
  "guide": [
    {
      "heading": "How the block works",
      "body": [
        "This is the mainly-strength block: 4 weeks with 6-8 working sets in total, followed by a deload. Each session is one main lift with its sets and reps for the week at a percentage of your 1RM.",
        "Rest 3-4 minutes between sets of the big compound lift.",
        "For the accessory work, repeat one of your favorite workouts from the 8 working set mesocycle of the Hypertrophy Block.",
        "The deadlift runs a week behind the other lifts, as heavy deadlifts should be done about once every 2 weeks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Week by week",
      "body": [
        "Weeks 1-2: 5x5 at 85% on every lift.",
        "Week 3: 3x3 at 90% on bench and rows (3x3 at 85% on overhead press), 3x2 at 90% on squats, and the deadlift stays at 5x5 at 85%.",
        "Week 4: a single at 100% on bench, rows and squats (a single at 90% on overhead press), light work on the second rows day, and 3x3 at 90% on deadlifts.",
        "Week 5: start your deload. The deadlift takes its single at 100%."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Deload",
      "body": [
        "Take a deload week, or 2-3 weeks of almost no lifting. On a lighter deload, each workout day is 5 sets of one exercise at 40% of your 1RM.",
        "Afterwards, start again at the beginning of the Hypertrophy Block with your new %RM."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Terms",
      "body": [
        "RIR = reps in reserve. If a set says 3 RIR, pick a weight and stop at a rep where you feel you could still push out 3 more reps.",
        "%1RM = percentage of your one-rep max. For 80%, take 80% of your one-rep max and use that weight."
      ]
    }
  ],
